   "textLength": 383,
   "text": "Control your spending – When you use a debit card to pay for things, you are spending the money in your account. If there's no money in the account, you can't make a purchase.\nLess risk of debt – Using a debit card is less risky than using a credit card, because you can't run up a debt. \nLower cost – Because you aren't borrowing money, you aren't paying interest on what you spend.",
